Watch files and re-run a task on changes

Usage: mk watch [OPTIONS] [TASK_NAME] [-- <TRAILING_ARGS>...]

Arguments:
  [TASK_NAME]
          The task name to run

  [TRAILING_ARGS]...
          Arguments forwarded to the task on each run (available as ${{ args.0 }}, ${{ args.1 }}, etc.)

Options:
      --label <FILTER>
          Watch tasks matching label (KEY or KEY=VALUE). Repeatable; all must match.

      --path <PATH>
          Override watched paths (repeatable; defaults to task inputs when absent)

      --debounce <DURATION>
          Debounce duration for filesystem event coalescing (e.g. 500ms, 1s, 2.5s)

      --clear
          Clear terminal before each rerun (default: append output)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  mk watch build
  mk watch build --path src --path Cargo.toml
  mk watch build --debounce 1s --clear
  mk watch --label ci --path src
